  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Prompt Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the prompt requirements, focusing on the \"ultra-mode\" stipulations, to formulate a solid verification plan. I\'m starting by mapping out the verification journeys, specifically outlining the core tasks and their expected behavior within the `ultra-mode` context. My goal is to create a detailed verification plan, covering all required journeys and their steps. I plan to refine the verification plan during the next iteration, making sure it addresses all potential edge cases.\n\n\n**Mapping Task Functionality**\n\nI\'ve just focused on mapping out specific task functionalities and how they persist within the application. I tested the process of creating a new task, linking repositories with custom branches, and verifying that the task\'s Git workflow stages persist even after reloading the browser. Following that, I explored the Task Detail view, testing several functionalities like adding changed files, test records (including passed and blocked), and screenshots, verifying their persistence. I\'m now moving on to the more complex elements of the process.\n\n\n**Testing UI and Functionality**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into UI testing. I\'ve started by examining the live task timer\'s persistence across views and after adding time manually. I\'m verifying the switch between Kanban and Table views and the filtering by repository. Next, I plan to toggle themes and explore the backup/restore features, including validation after each operation. I intend to thoroughly test the dashboard elements with real metrics, quick actions, and the activity timeline, along with the \"My Tasks\" view\'s search bar and filters to include their function with table and kanban views, and archive/recover features.\n\n\n**Defining Task Views**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the Task Detail View. It should be structured with eight tabs: Overview, Project & Workspace, Problem & Investigation, Changed Files, Screenshots & Attachments, Test Records, Workflow Stages, and Related Tasks. The Overview includes basic task info. The Project & Workspace tab outlines linked repositories. Problem & Investigation will capture details like root cause analysis. Changed Files will show file changes with diffs and notes, and the screenshot section provides a place to store images of before and after states. I will also make space for test records, workflows, and related task information.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now refining the data structures, specifically for the Task Detail View. I\'m focusing on the \"Screenshots & Attachments\" tab, ensuring a thumbnail gallery with a full-size zoom modal, side-by-side comparisons, and the ability to rename and delete images. Also, I\'m working on the \"Test Records\" section, and defining data points for title, type, steps, status, and related links. I\'m also ensuring the Git workflow stage visualization and time tracking elements are correctly integrated.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on data structures related to repositories, and remote definitions including base and development branches. I\'ve also begun designing the format for work logs, including daily and weekly summaries, session logs, and exportable summaries. I\'m moving on to settings: theme preferences, timezone handling, and custom cloud target naming for Git workflows. I\'ll include the specifications for tag management, attachment limits, and demo dataset loading and removal. Finally, I\'m defining full backup export (JSON bundle with base64 encoded data) and restore functionalities.\n\n\n**Structuring Project Components**\n\nI\'m now determining the optimal project structure. I\'m evaluating two primary approaches: either integrating the core backend and database directly within the root, or encapsulating the full project within the `/MIHIR/` directory, while the root server mounts and serves the app on port 3000. I need to make sure this facilitates both the AI Studio preview and the end user requirements for the deliverable.\n\n\n"
