cess worked flawlessly on the initial attempt. Also, I\'ve identified the root cause of the \\\"tsx: not found\\\" error: `tsx` is indeed installed locally within `./node_modules/.bin/tsx`. Now, my next step is to execute `./node_modules/.bin/tsx` to continue the workflow.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"./node_modules/.bin/tsx --test MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.test.ts MIHIR/server/db.test.ts\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running unit and SQLite persistence tests with local tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run unit tests with tsx\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting dev server to serve full-stack Express + SQLite + Vite app\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server\\\"\",\"waitForPreviousTools\":\"true\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":74,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-21T12:45:27Z\",\"input_tokens\":2912,\"cache_read_tokens\":198134,\"output_tokens\":432,\"thinking\":\"**Verifying browser behavior**\\n\\nI\'m pleased to report that all six unit and SQLite persistence tests have passed. Now I\'m shifting focus to Browser Verification Round 1. I\'m leveraging `playwright-cli` within the `ultra-mode` and `computer-use` context, with the aim to capture the first paint at desktop size.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT\\\\nmkdir -p .playwright-cli && \\\\\\\\\\\\n  playwright-cli open --browser=chromium http://localhost:3000 && \\\\\\\\\\\\n  playwright-cli resize 1440 900 && \\\\\\\\\\\\n  playwright-cli screenshot --filename=.playwright-cli/r1-desktop.png && \\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\n<truncated 221 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Capturing desktop and mobile screenshots and console logs\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Capture r1 screensho