  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Evidence**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the images, specifically `r1-task-git.png` and `r1-projects-repos.png`. Focusing on the first image, I\'ve noticed a \"Delivery Readiness & Explicit Task Completion\" gate. It\'s showing \"Complete Task (1 Checks Remaining)\". This indicates the current stage of the task.\n\n\n**Observing Repository Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the repository details. I can see the \"raydashboard\" project with its local path and remote URL in `r1-projects-repos.png`. It also shows the `development2` as the Dev Target. The distinct summary cards in `r1-task-git.png` give a clear view of where the process is. The `/Users/mihir/workspace/ray/raydashboard` local path is displayed with a Copy Path button and the 14-stage stepper.\n\n\n**Addressing Scroll Retention**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a crucial UI flaw related to scroll position. Specifically, in `MihirWorkspaceApp.tsx`, the `<main>` container, despite being `overflow-y-auto`, retains its previous `scrollTop` when changing the `activeNav` or `selectedTaskId`. I\'m thinking of adding a `mainRef` to `<main>` to reset the scroll position to the top whenever `activeNav`, `selectedTaskId`, or `selectedTaskTab` changes. This should address the undesired scroll preservation observed, particularly in the `Projects & Repositories` view. Also, I\'m checking the Critique Checklist for any other fixes.\n\n\n"
