  planner_response {
    response: "I have built **MIHIR Workspace**, your personal developer task tracker, engineering investigation journal, and multi-repository Git workflow tracker for the **Ray** project inside the `/MIHIR` directory.\n\n### Key Capabilities & Architecture (`/MIHIR`)\n- **Persistent SQLite & Disk Storage (`/MIHIR/data` & `/MIHIR/uploads`)**:\n  - Uses Node\'s built-in `node:sqlite` (`MIHIR/data/mihir_workspace.sqlite`) to persist tasks, multi-repository branch configurations, 14-stage Git workflows, changed file inventories, test verification records, time entries, work notes, activity history, and workspace settings.\n  - Persists uploaded screenshots and verification attachments directly to disk in `MIHIR/uploads/`.\n- **Dashboard & Real-Time Metrics**:\n  - Displays live task metrics computed from stored data (`Assigned Active`, `In Progress`, `Blocked`, `Testing / Review`, `Awaiting Push/Merge`, `Completed`, `Overdue`, and `Time Today / Week`).\n  - Features a **Continue Working** feed with direct section jump links (`Investigation`, `Changed Files`, `Screenshots`, `Tests`, `Git Stepper`), project/repository filters, live persistent task timer, and an engineering activity timeline.\n- **Task List (Table & Kanban Views)**:\n  - Supports instant switching between **Table View** and **7-column Kanban Board** (`Backlog`, `Assigned`, `In Progress`, `Blocked`, `Ready for Testing`, `In Review`, `Done`), keeping task status decoupled from Git/deployment progress.\n  - Full search and filtering across task ID (`MIHIR-001`), title, branch (`RAY-MIHIR-...`), repository (`raydashboard`, `rayhubapp`, `rayjobapp`), changed file path, status, priority, tags, and dates, plus task duplication, archiving, and recovery.\n- **Dedicated Task Detail Workspace (7 Structured Sections)**:\n  - **A & B. Overview & Multi-Repository Context**: Tracks ticket URL, assignee metadata, acceptance criteria, blocker notes, and multiple repositories (`raydashboard`, `rayhubapp`, `rayjobapp`) with one-click local path copy, base branch (`development` / `development2`), working branch, dev target, and cloud target.\n  - **C. Issue & Investigation Journal**: Structured fields for problem summary, reproduction steps, root cause analysis, investigation notes, final solution, and key learnings with Markdown & code block preview.\n  - **D. Changed Files Inventory**: Per-file documentation of repository, relative path (with copy button), change type (`Added`, `Modified`, `Deleted`, `Renamed`, `Config Change`), what/why changed, code snippet, commit reference, and test notes.\n  - **E. Screenshots & Attachments**: Supports file picker, drag-and-drop, and clipboard paste (`Ctrl+V`) with categories (`Before`, `After`, `Bug Evidence`, `Test Result`, `Deployment Confirmation`), full-screen zoom modal, and interactive **Side-by-Side / Split-Slider Before & After Visual Comparison**.\n  - **F. Testing & Verification**: Tracks Unit, Integration, Manual, API, UI, Regression, and Build checks (`Not Run`, `Passed`, `Failed`, `Blocked`, `Skipped`) where `Blocked` tests never count as passed and block completion readiness until resolved.\n  - **G. 14-Stage Git & Deployment Workflow Stepper**: Tracks all 14 stages per repository (`PR-Based` or `Direct Merge` mode), distinguishes **Local Commit**, **Remote Push**, **Dev Branch Merge**, and **Cloud / Release Target** in separate summary cards, and enforces a configurable **Delivery Readiness Gate**.\n  - **H. Time Tracking & Activity History**: Persistent single-active-task timer, manual time entry editor, and Markdown engineering report export (`.md`).\n- **Sample Ray Dataset & Backup/Restore**:\n  - Preloaded with 4 clearly labeled sample Ray tasks (`MIHIR-001` through `MIHIR-004`) that can be removed or restored with one click from the Dashboard or Settings, alongside full JSON + base64 attachment backup export and validated restore.\n\n### Verification Summary\n- **Unit Tests**: Verified 5 test suites in `MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.test.ts` via `tsx --test` covering `Asia/Kolkata` unambiguous date formatting (`DD Mon YYYY`), `Blocked` test readiness gating, 14-stage Git workflow summary separation, branch/file-path filtering, and dashboard metric aggregation.\n- **Browser & Viewport Verification**: Verified in headless Chromium across desktop (`1440x900`) and mobile (`390x844`) viewports with zero console or network errors across Dashboard, Kanban/Table views, Task Detail (`Screenshots` Before/After comparison and `Git & Release` 14-stage stepper), Projects & Repositories, Work Log, and Settings (Light & Dark themes). Fixed scroll restoration on view navigation (`MihirWorkspaceApp.tsx`) so switching sections always starts at the top of the viewport."
    thinking: "**Examining Design Consistency**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the design consistency across different views. I\'m focusing on the light and dark modes, mobile and desktop formats, and especially the use of SQLite persistence. I\'ve also identified unit tests and file storage implementations. I am also working to check for consistency with the provided data files.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have built **MIHIR Workspace**, your personal developer task tracker, engineering investigation journal, and multi-repository Git workflow tracker for the **Ray** project inside the `/MIHIR` directory.\n\n### Key Capabilities & Architecture (`/MIHIR`)\n- **Persistent SQLite & Disk Storage (`/MIHIR/data` & `/MIHIR/uploads`)**:\n  - Uses Node\'s built-in `node:sqlite` (`MIHIR/data/mihir_workspace.sqlite`) to persist tasks, multi-repository branch configurations, 14-stage Git workflows, changed file inventories, test verification records, time entries, work notes, activity history, and workspace settings.\n  - Persists uploaded screenshots and verification attachments directly to disk in `MIHIR/uploads/`.\n- **Dashboard & Real-Time Metrics**:\n  - Displays live task metrics computed from stored data (`Assigned Active`, `In Progress`, `Blocked`, `Testing / Review`, `Awaiting Push/Merge`, `Completed`, `Overdue`, and `Time Today / Week`).\n  - Features a **Continue Working** feed with direct section jump links (`Investigation`, `Changed Files`, `Screenshots`, `Tests`, `Git Stepper`), project/repository filters, live persistent task timer, and an engineering activity timeline.\n- **Task List (Table & Kanban Views)**:\n  - Supports instant switching between **Table View** and **7-column Kanban Board** (`Backlog`, `Assigned`, `In Progress`, `Blocked`, `Ready for Testing`, `In Review`, `Done`), keeping task status decoupled from Git/deployment progress.\n  - Full search and filtering across task ID (`MIHIR-001`), title, branch (`RAY-MIHIR-...`), repository (`raydashboard`, `rayhubapp`, `rayjobapp`), changed file path, status, priority, tags, and dates, plus task duplication, archiving, and recovery.\n- **Dedicated Task Detail Workspace (7 Structured Sections)**:\n  - **A & B. Overview & Multi-Repository Context**: Tracks ticket URL, assignee metadata, acceptance criteria, blocker notes, and multiple repositories (`raydashboard`, `rayhubapp`, `rayjobapp`) with one-click local path copy, base branch (`development` / `development2`), working branch, dev target, and cloud target.\n  - **C. Issue & Investigation Journal**: Structured fields for problem summary, reproduction steps, root cause analysis, investigation notes, final solution, and key learnings with Markdown & code block preview.\n  - **D. Changed Files Inventory**: Per-file documentation of repository, relative path (with copy button), change type (`Added`, `Modified`, `Deleted`, `Renamed`, `Config Change`), what/why changed, code snippet, commit reference, and test notes.\n  - **E. Screenshots & Attachments**: Supports file picker, drag-and-drop, and clipboard paste (`Ctrl+V`) with categories (`Before`, `After`, `Bug Evidence`, `Test Result`, `Deployment Confirmation`), full-screen zoom modal, and interactive **Side-by-Side / Split-Slider Before & After Visual Comparison**.\n  - **F. Testing & Verification**: Tracks Unit, Integration, Manual, API, UI, Regression, and Build checks (`Not Run`, `Passed`, `Failed`, `Blocked`, `Skipped`) where `Blocked` tests never count as passed and block completion readiness until resolved.\n  - **G. 14-Stage Git & Deployment Workflow Stepper**: Tracks all 14 stages per repository (`PR-Based` or `Direct Merge` mode), distinguishes **Local Commit**, **Remote Push**, **Dev Branch Merge**, and **Cloud / Release Target** in separate summary cards, and enforces a configurable **Delivery Readiness Gate**.\n  - **H. Time Tracking & Activity History**: Persistent single-active-task timer, manual time entry editor, and Markdown engineering report export (`.md`).\n- **Sample Ray Dataset & Backup/Restore**:\n  - Preloaded with 4 clearly labeled sample Ray tasks (`MIHIR-001` through `MIHIR-004`) that can be removed or restored with one click from the Dashboard or Settings, alongside full JSON + base64 attachment backup export and validated restore.\n\n### Verification Summary\n- **Unit Tests**: Verified 5 test suites in `MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.test.ts` via `tsx --test` covering `Asia/Kolkata` unambiguous date formatting (`DD Mon YYYY`), `Blocked` test readiness gating, 14-stage Git workflow summary separation, branch/file-path filtering, and dashboard metric aggregation.\n- **Browser & Viewport Verification**: Verified in headless Chromium across desktop (`1440x900`) and mobile (`390x844`) viewports with zero console or network errors across Dashboard, Kanban/Table views, Task Detail (`Screenshots` Before/After comparison and `Git & Release` 14-stage stepper), Projects & Repositories, Work Log, and Settings (Light & Dark themes). Fixed scroll restoration on view navigation (`MihirWorkspaceApp.tsx`) so switching sections always starts at the top of the viewport."
