  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Current Context**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the loaded skills: `firebase-integration-rpc` and `gemini-api`. We provisioned Firebase in `firebase-integration-rpc` (project `hybrid-choir-0mn89`, database `ai-`. I\'m cross-referencing this against the requirements of the task to ensure these resources are suitable for the planned integration. I\'m keen to avoid unnecessary complexity.\n\n\n**Defining Firebase Integration**\n\nI\'m now outlining the precise workflow needed, mirroring `firebase-integration-rpc`. This involves setting up `firebase-blueprint.json` according to `FirebaseBlueprintConfig`, generating Firestore rules with all security checks, and initializing the Firebase SDK, making use of `firebase-applet-config.json`. Specifically, I am ensuring to use Firestore and Google Sign-In as required. I have decided to call the specific action `DeployRules`.\n\n\n**Designing User Sync Features**\n\nI\'m now mapping out how MIHIR Workspace will leverage Firebase Auth, Cloud Firestore, daily features, and the Gemini assistant. I\'m focusing on user sign-in via Google using `signInWithPopup` directly in the UI. Upon sign-in, local workspace data (tasks, projects, logs) will sync to Firestore in real-time using `onSnapshot`. First-time users can sync their workspace with a one-click option.\n\n\n**Developing AI Copilot Navigation**\n\nI\'m currently designing the AI Engineering Copilot. It\'ll have a dedicated view accessible through a navigation menu, plus a quick drawer accessible throughout the workspace, even while inspecting tasks! It\'ll keep a multi-turn conversation history, stored in SQLite and synced to Firestore when the user signs in. I\'m focusing on user-selectable Engineering Roles and Gemini Models.\n\n\n**Implementing Task Context**\n\nI am now focusing on integrating live task context from `rayhubapp` and `rayjobapp`. I plan to attach active tasks like `MIHIR-001`, `MIHIR-002`, and so on, directly into the system instruction for the chatbot. This will allow the AI to draft detailed notes and checklists. I am also planning a fallback to `gemini-3.8-flash` in case of free-tier key issues.\n\n**Enhancing Daily Features**\n\nI\'m working to upgrade daily use with a Command Palette (`\342\214\230K`/`Ctrl+K`) for quick navigation. There will be an interactive \"Daily Focus Checklist\" and a one-click \"Copy Daily Standup Report\" feature on the dashboard. I\'m aiming to make the copilot perfect for day-to-day use.\n\n\n**Generating Task Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating a \"Daily Standup\" button on both the Dashboard and Work Log, generating clean, formatted output. Additionally, I\'m working on a \"One-Click Git Command Generator\" within the Task Detail to eliminate friction in daily terminal work. I\'m prioritizing the \"Firebase Blueprint & Hardened Security Rules\" process as a crucial step for integration, as well as checking the exact schema requirements for `firebase-blueprint.json` to ensure everything is streamlined.\n\n\n**Structuring Firestore Entities**\n\nI\'m now detailing the data structures for Firestore. I\'m carefully avoiding JSON strings, as I have been directed, opting for native maps, lists (with bounded array sizes), and dedicated collections. My focus is on creating clean, well-structured entities to facilitate efficient storage and retrieval. This includes entities such as `UserWorkspaceTask`, `WorkspaceNote`, `WorkspaceTimeEntry`, `ChatThread` and `ChatMessage`.\n\n\n**Validating Chat Message Structures**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on message structures within `chatThreads/{threadId}/messages/{messageId}`. I\'m confirming subcollection compliance against \"Pillar 1,\" verifying thread ownership via `get()` and ensuring bounded arrays within `WorkspaceTask`. I am creating and updating validation functions like `isValidChatMessage(data)` for data integrity. The focus is ensuring the schema conforms to the Eight Pillars for security.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Security Checks**\n\nI\'m now implementing granular security checks on all operations within `chatThreads/{threadId}/messages/{messageId}`. I\'m focusing on \"Pillar 4\" and \"Pillar 5\" - ensuring all updates are action-based and guarding against unbounded arrays using functions like `isValidChatMessage(data)` on `get`, `create`, `update`, and `delete`. I\'m meticulously applying these principles. The focus is ensuring the schema conforms to the Eight Pillars for security.\n\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1343702"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"{\\n  \\\"entities\\\": {\\n    \\\"WorkspaceTask\\\": {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"WorkspaceTask\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"A developer task tracked in MIHIR Workspace for the Ray project.\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"ownerId\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Firebase Auth UID of the task owner.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n          \\\"maxLength\\\": 128,\\n          \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\\\\\\\-]+$\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"taskCode\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Human-readable task identifier such as MIHIR-001.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n          \\\"maxLength\\\": 40,\\n          \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\\\\\\\-]+$\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"title\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Task title.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n          \\\"maxLength\\\": 300\\n        },\\n        \\\"description\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Detailed task description and requirements.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 0,\\n          \\\"maxLength\\\": 5000\\n        },\\n        \\\"projectName\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Project name such as Ray.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n          \\\"maxLength\\\": 120\\n        },\\n        \\\"repositoryName\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Primary repository name such as raydashboard, rayhubapp, or rayjobapp.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n          \\\"maxLength\\\": 120\\n        },\\n        \\\"workingBranch\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Working Git branch name.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n          \\\"maxLength\\\": 200\\n        },\\n        \\\"baseBranch\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Base Git branch name.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n          \\\"maxLength\\\": 200\\n        },\\n        \\\"status\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Current workflow status of the task.\\\",\\n          \\\"enum\\\": [\\n            \\\"Backlog\\\",\\n            \\\"Assigned\\\",\\n            \\\"In Progress\\\",\\n            \\\"Blocked\\\",\\n            \\\"Ready for Testing\\\",\\n            \\\"In Review\\\",\\n            \\\"Done\\\",\\n            \\\"Locked\\\"\\n          ],\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n          \\\"maxLength\\\": 40\\n        },\\n        \\\"priority\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Task priority level.\\\",\\n          \\\"enum\\\": [\\\"Low\\\", \\\"Medium\\\", \\\"High\\\", \\\"Urgent\\\"],\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n          \\\"maxLength\\\": 20\\n        },\\n        \\\"rootCauseSummary\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Summary of root cause and final engineering solution.\\\",\\n          \\\"minLength\\\": 0,\\n          \\\"maxLength\\\": 5000\\n        },\\n        \\\"gitCompletedSteps\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Number of completed Git workflow steps (0 to 14).\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"gitTotalSteps\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Total number of Git workflow steps.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"isArchived\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether the task is archived.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"tags\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n          \