"\\\"/.playwright-cli/r1-tasks-kanban.png\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Inspecting Kanban board screenshot\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Inspect r1-tasks-kanban.png\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/MIHIR/src/components/TaskListView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"260\",\"StartLine\":\"170\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking TaskListView row click handlers\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check TaskListView.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":143,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-21T12:57:58Z\",\"input_tokens\":4557,\"cache_read_tokens\":50234,\"output_tokens\":110,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/MIHIR/src/components/TaskListView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"460\",\"StartLine\":\"350\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking Table View row rendering in TaskListView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View Table View rows\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":145,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-21T12:58:10Z\",\"input_tokens\":2315,\"cache_read_tokens\":54792,\"output_tokens\":954,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing the Failure**\\n\\nI\'ve uncovered the root cause of the click failure. It seems the `getByText(\\\"MIHIR-001\\\")` selector in `TaskListView.tsx` is matching the filter placeholder text, on line 200, or some other match. My original expectation, to target the button, was incorrect. I need a more specific selector, avoiding the placeholder ambiguity, to ensure the intended element is clicked.\\n\\n\\n**Verifying the Button**\\n\\nI\'ve determined that `getByRole(\'button\', { name: \'MIHIR-001\' })` precisely targets the\\n<truncated 27 bytes>\\ntable! Now I\'m shifting focus to verify the remaining visual elements. I\'m carefully reviewing the mobile dashboard layout in `r1-dashboard-mobile.png`, observing its readability and lack of horizontal scroll. I\'m also examining the Kanban board in `r1-tasks-kanban.png`, particularly the responsive grid layout of the status columns. I will perform the second round of verification using the new selector to inspect Task Detail, Projects & Repositories, and Settings. I plan to click \\\"Restore Demo Data\\\" too.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT\\\\nplaywright-cli open --browser=chromium http://localhost:3000\\\\nplaywright-cli resize 1440 900\\\\nsleep 1\\\\nplaywright-cli run-code \'async (page) => {\\\\n  await page.getByRole(\\\\\\\"button\\\\\\\", { name: /My Tasks/i }).click();\\\\n  awai\\n<truncated 1189 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Capturing Task Detail tabs, Projects & Repos, and Light Theme Settings\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Capture Task Detail and Settings views\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":147,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-21T12:58:38Z\",\"input_tokens\":3577,\"cache_read_tokens\":55058,\"output_tokens\":108,\"content\":\"I am running the browser verification across the Task Detail sections (`Screenshots & Attachments` and `Git & Deployment`), `Projects & Repositories`, and `Settings` (including Light/Dark theme switching). I will inspect the screenshots once the capture finishes.\"}\n{\"step_index\":149,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-21T12:59:07Z\",\"input_tokens\":2660,\"cache_read_tokens\":56586,\"output_tokens\":270,\"thinking\":\"**Investigating Click Failure**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on why a specific button click isn\'t navigating to the expected Task Detail view. I\'m digging into `TaskDetailView.tsx` and `MihirWorkspaceApp.tsx` to understand the routing and event handling for these interactions. The `getByRole` selectors aren\'t cooperating as expected and I\'m looking into how the `name` attribute is