  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Core Request**: Update the UI in the Task List view (`MIHIR/src/components/TaskListView.tsx`) to include a visual progress indicator for tasks that have sub-tasks or defined checklist items.\n   - **Success Criteria**:\n     - Tasks can have structured sub-tasks / checklist items (and/or parsed checklist lines from `acceptanceCriteria` / dedicated `subtasks: TaskChecklistItem[]` array on `TaskRecord`).\n     - In `TaskListView.tsx` (both **Table View** and **Kanban Board** view), any task with sub-tasks or defined checklist items displays a clear visual progress indicator (e.g., completed/total count `3/5`, percentage `60%`, segmented or smooth progress bar with color coding such as emerald at 100%, indigo in-progress, and interactive or expandable preview / quick toggle if helpful).\n     - Users can also view, add, toggle, and remove sub-tasks / checklist items in `TaskDetailView.tsx` (Overview tab) and `NewTaskModal.tsx`, and existing demo tasks in `MIHIR/server/seedDemoData.ts` include realistic Ray sub-tasks/checklist items so the visual progress indicator is immediately visible on load.\n     - Pure logic for computing sub-task/checklist progress is decoupled in `MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.ts` and covered by unit tests in `MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.test.ts`.\n     - Verified in a real headless browser via `playwright-cli` (`computer-use` + `ultra-mode` skills) across desktop (`1440x900`) and mobile (`390x844`) viewports with zero console/page errors.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed in Prior Turns**:\n     - Full MIHIR Workspace application (`MIHIR/src/MihirWorkspaceApp.tsx`), SQLite persistence (`MIHIR/server/db.ts`), Express API (`MIHIR/server/apiRouter.ts`), Firebase Auth + Cloud Firestore sync (`MIHIR/src/lib/firebaseClient.ts`, `firestore.rules`, `firebase-blueprint.json`), Multi-turn Gemini Engineering Copilot (`MIHIR/src/components/AiCopilotView.tsx`), Command Palette (`MIHIR/src/components/CommandPaletteModal.tsx`), and Dashboard Daily Focus (`MIHIR/src/components/DashboardView.tsx`).\n   - **Completed in Current Turn**:\n     - Inspected `MIHIR/src/components/TaskListView.tsx` (lines 1\342\200\223520), `MIHIR/src/types/workspace.ts` (lines 1\342\200\223246), and `MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.ts` (lines 1\342\200\223280).\n   - **In Progress / Incomplete**:\n     - Viewing lines 520\342\200\223645 of `MIHIR/src/components/TaskListView.tsx` (Kanban board rendering), `MIHIR/src/components/TaskDetailView.tsx`, and `MIHIR/server/seedDemoData.ts`.\n     - Adding `TaskSubtaskItem` / checklist support to `TaskRecord` and `summarizeSubtaskProgress(task)` in `MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.ts`.\n     - Updating `TaskListView.tsx` (both Table View and Kanban Board cards) to render the visual progress indicator for tasks with sub-tasks or checklist items.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - **Existing `TaskRecord` Schema (`MIHIR/src/types/workspace.ts`)**:\n     - Currently has `acceptanceCriteria: string` (often multi-line bullet/checklist items) and `tests: TaskTestRecord[]` and `repositories: TaskRepository[]`, but does not yet have an explicit `subtasks?: TaskSubtaskItem[]` array field.\n     - Supporting **both** an explicit `subtasks?: TaskSubtaskItem[]` array (`{ id: string; title: string; completed: boolean }`) AND fallback parsing of Markdown/bullet lines in `acceptanceCriteria` (or seeding `subtasks` on the 4 demo tasks in `MIHIR/server/seedDemoData.ts` + migrating existing SQLite tasks in `MIHIR/server/db.ts` if `subtasks` is empty) ensures that both existing tasks and newly created tasks have rich sub-task checklist items.\n   - **SQLite Storage (`MIHIR/server/db.ts`)**:\n     - Tasks are stored with a `data_json` JSON column in the `tasks` SQLite table (`getFullWorkspaceState` parses `data_json`), which makes adding `subtasks: TaskSubtaskItem[]` to `TaskRecord` seamless without destructive SQLite schema changes.\n   - **TaskListView Structure (`MIHIR/src/components/TaskListView.tsx`)**:\n     - Has two view modes: `\'table\'` (lines 373\342\200\223540) and `\'kanban\'` (lines 541\342\200\223645).\n     - In `\'table\'` mode, each row currently shows `Task ID`, `Title & Context`, `Task Status`, `Priority`, `Repositories & Branches`, `Git & Release Progress`, `Due / Updated`, and `Actions`. We can display the **Sub-tasks & Checklist Progress** visual indicator directly inside the `Title & Context` column (or a dedicated column / inline progress bar with checklist icon, `completed/total` count, percentage badge, and interactive quick-check or tooltip) AND on each Kanban card in `\'kanban\'` mode.\n\n4. **Active Context**\n   - Dev server is running on `http://localhost:3000` via root `server.ts` (`MIHIR/server/apiRouter.ts` + Vite middleware).\n   - Firestore database `ai-studio-mihirworkspace-9782de47-d45e-447b-963b-7b19491e18a1` has deployed security rules (`firestore.rules`). Note: if `firebaseClient.ts` syncs tasks to Firestore `tasks/{taskId}`, check `firestore.rules` `isValidWorkspaceTask` \342\200\224 `firestore.rules` strictly allowlists keys on the `tasks` collection (`hasOnly(...)`). Therefore, keep the Firestore payload keys in `syncTaskToFirestore` (`MIHIR/src/lib/firebaseClient.ts`) unchanged (or if adding fields to Firestore, update `firebase-blueprint.json` + `firestore.rules` + redeploy). Keeping `syncTaskToFirestore`\'s outgoing Firestore document keys unchanged avoids unnecessary rule churn while storing `subtasks` in local SQLite + UI state.\n\n5. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Read Remaining Files**:\n      - View lines 520\342\200\223645 of `MIHIR/src/components/TaskListView.tsx`, `MIHIR/src/components/TaskDetailView.tsx` (Overview section), and `MIHIR/server/seedDemoData.ts` + `MIHIR/server/db.ts`.\n   2. **Add Data Model & Pure Progress Logic**:\n      - In `MIHIR/src/types/workspace.ts`, add `export interface TaskSubtaskItem { id: string; title: string; completed: boolean; }` and add `subtasks?: TaskSubtaskItem[];` to `TaskRecord`.\n      - In `MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.ts`, implement `summarizeTaskChecklistProgress(task: TaskRecord)` which computes `{ total: number; completed: number; percent: number; hasItems: boolean; items: TaskSubtaskItem[] }` from `task.subtasks` (with automatic fallback to parsing non-empty checklist lines from `task.acceptanceCriteria` if `task.subtasks` is undefined/empty).\n      - Add unit tests in `MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.test.ts` verifying `summarizeTaskChecklistProgress` for tasks with subtasks, tasks with acceptance criteria checklist lines, completed state (100%), partial state, and tasks with 0 items.\n   3. **Seed Demo Subtasks & Wire API/Detail View**:\n      - Update `MIHIR/server/seedDemoData.ts` (and `MIHIR/server/db.ts` normalization) so `MIHIR-001`, `MIHIR-002`, `MIHIR-003`, and `MIHIR-004` have realistic Ray engineering sub-tasks/checklist items with varied completion percentages (e.g. `4/4 (100%)`, `2/4 (50%)`, `3/4 (75%)`, `1/3 (33%)`).\n      - Update `MIHIR/src/components/TaskDetailView.tsx` (Overview tab) and `MIHIR/src/components/NewTaskModal.tsx` so users can add, toggle, and delete sub-tasks/checklist items.\n      - Also allow quick-toggling sub-task checkboxes or expanding sub-tasks directly from `TaskListView.tsx` (wired to `onUpdateTask` in `MihirWorkspaceApp.tsx`).\n   4. **Update `TaskListView.tsx` UI (Table & Kanban)**:\n      - Render a clear, high-craft visual progress indicator on every task that has sub-tasks or checklist items in both **Table View** and **Kanban Board** view (showing a `CheckSquare`/`ListChecks` icon, `completed/total` tabular count, `percent%`, a smooth progress bar colored emerald when 100% complete or indigo when in progress, and an expandable/interactive sub-task checklist preview).\n   5. **Verify & Test**:\n      - Run `npx tsx --test firestore.rules.test.ts MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.test.ts`.\n      - Run `compile_applet` and `restart_dev_server`.\n      - Open `http://localhost:3000` with `playwright-cli`, navigate to `My Tasks`, verify both Table View and Kanban Board visual progress indicators on desktop (`1440x900`) and mobile (`390x844`), inspect screenshots via `view_file`, and confirm zero console/network errors.\n\n6. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Follow `ultra-mode` and `frontend-design` rules: no `window.alert`/`window.confirm`, use `tabular-nums` for all counters/percentages, keep text labels crisp with `whitespace-nowrap` on badges, and verify the live rendered DOM and screenshots with `playwright-cli` before finishing.\n</summary>"
