  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Solution**\n\nI\'m focusing now on designing a clean and thorough solution to the UI update request. The core of it involves adding visual progress indicators to tasks with sub-tasks or checklists. I\'m aiming for a design that\'s intuitive and informative. I want to balance clarity with visual appeal.\n\n\n**Implementing the Types**\n\nI\'ve defined the necessary data structures in `/MIHIR/src/types/workspace.ts`. I added `TaskChecklistItem` and incorporated a `subtasks` field into `TaskRecord`. In addition, I created a `TaskChecklistProgressSummary` interface to streamline progress calculations. Now, I\'m integrating the logic in `/MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.ts`, including the methods to parse checklists and summarize task progress.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now refining how the data structures handle checklist items. I\'m prioritizing the logic for parsing checklists from the `acceptanceCriteria` field, handling different checklist formats, and defaulting completed items based on the task status. My focus is on robust parsing and accurate progress computation.\n\n\n**Calculating Task Progress**\n\nI\'m now focusing on calculating task progress accurately using real-world examples. I\'m looking at tasks like `MIHIR-001`, `MIHIR-002`, and `MIHIR-003` to validate my checklist parsing logic. I\'m focusing on parsing checklists, dealing with varied completion, and making sure the calculation accurately reflects the completeness of the subtasks.\n\n\n**Validating Checklist Logic**\n\nI\'m now validating checklist parsing and progress calculations with real examples like `MIHIR-004`. I\'m verifying the system correctly represents completion percentages based on task statuses and handling varied completion scenarios, including dealing with tasks that were created before the \"subtasks\" field existed in the database. I\'m focusing on ensuring robust parsing and accurate progress computation.\n\n\n**Integrating Subtasks Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating the subtasks data handling into the API, making sure that both the `POST /api/tasks` and `POST /api/tasks/:id/duplicate` routes preserve the `subtasks` field. I\'m also modifying the `TaskListView` to accept an `onToggleSubtask` prop and incorporate a detailed sub-tasks and checklist progress block within the Table View, including the header row with a `ListChecks` icon, completed/total count, a percentage badge and a toggle to expand/collapse the subtasks. I want a segmented or smooth visual progress bar.\n\n\n**Visualizing Task Progress**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI enhancements. I\'m focusing on incorporating accessible ARIA attributes and a visual progress bar with segment markers to show checklist progress, which is intuitive and informative. When the sub-tasks are expanded, I want users to toggle sub-task completion directly within the Task List. In Kanban view, I\'m working to integrate a compact progress indicator with a mini-checklist preview for quick task updates.\n\n\n"
