  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visuals of Tasks**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the visual representations of the task progress views. The Table View screenshots especially (`tasks-table-progress.png` & `tasks-table-expanded.png`) show a crisp presentation of task data in each row, with a focus on progress. I need to understand what information is immediately clear.\n\n\n**Observing Progress Displays**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the visual nuances of progress representation within the sub-task card. The progress bar looks good, and I\'m interested in how well the progress is communicated at a glance, from the `3/4 (75%)` and similar indicators to the completion squares. I also saw that the table overflows at 1440px viewport. I\'m now thinking about how to improve the table layout to prevent this.\n\n\n"
