  planner_response {
    response: "I have updated the Task List view (`My Tasks`) and task data model in **MIHIR Workspace** to include a visual progress indicator for tasks with sub-tasks or defined checklist items:\n\n- **Visual Progress Indicator in Table & Kanban Views**:\n  - Tasks with sub-tasks or structured acceptance criteria checklists display a **Sub-tasks / Checklist** progress card in both **Table View** and **Kanban Board** view.\n  - Shows the completed/total count (e.g., `3/5`, `4/4`) and completion percentage (`60%`, `100%`) in `tabular-nums`, paired with an accessible progress bar (`role=\"progressbar\"`), segmented item status dots, and a preview of the next pending sub-task (or `\342\234\223 All checklist items verified` in emerald when 100% complete).\n  - Clicking **Sub-tasks** expands the interactive checklist inline in the Task List or Kanban card so you can check or uncheck individual sub-tasks directly without leaving the list view.\n- **Task Detail & Creation Support**:\n  - Added a **Sub-tasks & Execution Checklist** section in the Task Detail **Overview & Workspace** tab to add, toggle, and remove checklist items, as well as a **Sub-tasks / Checklist Items** input in the **New Task** modal."
