  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Assessing Core Skillsets**\n\nI\'m currently focused on evaluating how existing skillsets, like frontend design and computer use, are performing in ultra-mode. My analysis is progressing well, with clear distinctions emerging regarding proficiency levels. This is critical for making informed decisions.\n\n\n**Defining Board Workflow**\n\nI\'m now carefully mapping out the logic for the new board view. Specifically, I\'m defining the relationship between task statuses in the Mihir Workspace and the four columns in the drag-and-drop board. I\'m focusing on how task status changes as they are moved between columns, like \"Todo\" and \"In Progress.\" This should result in a clear, pure function for status mapping.\n\n\n**Implementing Board Functionality**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation details for the drag-and-drop board. I\'m focusing on defining pure functions within `MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.ts` and their corresponding unit tests in `MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.test.ts`. Specifically, I\'m working on `resolveStatusFromBoardColumnDrop`, the function which will manage changes in status triggered by movement between columns. I am also working on `mapStatusToBoardColumn` to ensure that there is a proper association of each task.\n\n\n**Designing Board Navigation**\n\nI\'m now thinking about user experience related to the board view within `TaskListView`. I\'m designing the default behavior when a user selects the \"Board View\" toggle: the 4-column layout (Todo, In Progress, Review, Done) will be displayed. I\'m also considering an optional sub-toggle within Board View to switch between the 4-column workflow and the 7-status column grid to maintain all functionality. Finally, I\'m thinking about full HTML5 drag-and-drop support alongside keyboard/click quick-move controls and drag feedback.\n\n\n**Visualizing Board Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user feedback during drag-and-drop actions. I\'m visualizing the dragged card with reduced opacity, scaling, and a subtle ring, and highlighting the drop target with a dashed border and surface tint. Upon dropping a card, I will invoke `onUpdateTaskStatus`, which persists status changes to SQLite and logs the activity. Each card in the Board View will display a drag handle, task code badge, status pill, priority badge, and more.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
