  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Board Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the board. I\'m starting by defining the `BoardWorkflowColumnId` type to represent columns like \"Todo,\" \"In Progress,\" \"Review,\" and \"Done.\" This is now extending to `BoardWorkflowColumnDefinition` and `BOARD_WORKFLOW_COLUMNS` to provide a complete board column mapping and drag-and-drop helpers in the file `/MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.ts`.\n\n\n**Implementing Board Column Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing functions to map task statuses to board columns and resolve new statuses from column drops. I\'ve defined `mapStatusToBoardColumn`, `resolveStatusFromBoardColumnDrop`, and `groupTasksByBoardColumn`, and am now working on tests. I\'m also updating `/MIHIR/src/components/TaskListView.tsx` to include a view mode switcher and a 4-column workflow view. I\'m focusing on lines 155-205 in that file, and will soon address the 7-stage detailed view toggle as well.\n\n\n**Designing Drag-and-Drop**\n\nI\'m currently designing the drag-and-drop interaction for the board. I\'m focusing on HTML5 drag-and-drop for both board modes and a programmatic quick-move control. Each column will be a drop zone with specific data-testid attributes. Cards will be draggable, setting dataTransfer data and `draggedTaskId`. I\'m working on highlighting the drop target and handling the status resolution upon a drop, including visual confirmations. Each card will also feature a drag handle, task code, priority badge, and status indicator.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1163284"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Add 4-column Board View mapping and drag-and-drop status resolution functions to workspaceLogic.ts\", \"EndLine\":643, \"Instruction\":\"Append BoardWorkflowColumnId, BOARD_WORKFLOW_COLUMNS, mapStatusToBoardColumn, resolveStatusFromBoardColumnDrop, and groupTasksByBoardColumn to workspaceLogic.ts\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"  lines.push(``, `## 5. Testing & Verification (${task.tests.length})`);\\n  for (const t of task.tests) {\\n    lines.push(\\n      `- **[${t.status}] ${t.title}** (${t.testType}) \342\200\224 Command/Steps: \\\\`${t.commandOrSteps}\\\\``,\\n      `  - *Expected:* ${t.expectedResult}`,\\n      `  - *Actual:* ${t.actualResult}${t.blockedOrSkippedReason ? ` (Reason: ${t.blockedOrSkippedReason})` : \'\'}`\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  return lines.join(\'\\\\n\');\\n}\\n\\nexport type BoardWorkflowColumnId = \'Todo\' | \'In Progress\' | \'Review\' | \'Done\';\\n\\nexport interface BoardWorkflowColumnDefinition {\\n  id: BoardWorkflowColumnId;\\n  label: string;\\n  subtitle: string;\\n  mappedStatuses: TaskStatus[];\\n  defaultDropStatus: TaskStatus;\\n}\\n\\nexport const BOARD_WORKFLOW_COLUMNS: BoardWorkflowColumnDefinition[] = [\\n  {\\n    id: \'Todo\',\\n    label: \'Todo\',\\n    subtitle: \'Backlog & Assigned\',\\n    mappedStatuses: [\'Backlog\', \'Assigned\'],\\n    defaultDropStatus: \'Assigned\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'In Progress\',\\n    label: \'In Progress\',\\n    subtitle: \'Active & Blocked\',\\n    mappedStatuses: [\'In Progress\', \'Blocked\'],\\n    defaultDropStatus: \'In Progress\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'Review\',\\n    label: \'Review\',\\n    subtitle: \'Testing & Code Review\',\\n    mappedStatuses: [\'Ready for Testing\', \'In Review\'],\\n    defaultDropStatus: \'In Review\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'Done\',\\n    label: \'Done\',\\n    subtitle: \'Verified & Merged\',\\n    mappedStatuses: [\'Done\'],\\n    defaultDropStatus: \'Done\',\\n  },\\n];\\n\\nexport function mapStatusToBoardColumn(status: TaskStatus): BoardWorkflowColumnId {\\n  switch (status) {\\n    case \'Backlog\':\\n    case \'Assigned\':\\n      return \'Todo\';\\n    case \'In Progress\':\\n    case \'Blocked\':\\n      return \'In Progress\';\\n    case \'Ready for Testing\':\\n    case \'In Review\':\\n      return \'Review\';\\n    case \'Done\':\\n      return \'Done\';\\n    default:\\n      return \'Todo\';\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function resolveStatusFromBoardColumnDrop(\\n  targetColumnId: BoardWorkflowColumnId,\\n  currentStatus?: TaskStatus\\n): TaskStatus {\\n  const column = BOARD_WORKFLOW_COLUMNS.find((c) => c.id === targetColumnId);\\n  if (!column) {\\n    return currentStatus ?? \'Assigned\';\\n  }\\n  if (currentStatus && column.mappedStatuses.includes(currentStatus)) {\\n    return currentStatus;\\n  }\\n  return column.defaultDropStatus;\\n}\\n\\nexport function groupTasksByBoardColumn(\\n  tasks: TaskRecord[]\\n): Record<BoardWorkflowColumnId, TaskRecord[]> {\\n  const grouped: Record<BoardWorkflowColumnId, TaskRecord[]> = {\\n    Todo: [],\\n    \'In Progress\': [],\\n    Review: [],\\n    Done: [],\\n  };\\n\\n  for (const task of tasks) {\\n    const colId = mapStatusToBoardColumn(task.status);\\n    grouped[colId].push(task);\\n  }\\n\\n  return grouped;\\n}\\n\", \"StartLine\":630, \"TargetContent\":\"  lines.push(``, `## 5. Testing & Verification (${task.tests.length})`);\\n  for (const t of task.tests) {\\n    lines.push(\\n      `- **[${t.status}] ${t.title}** (${t.testType}) \342\200\224 Command/Steps: \\\\`${t.commandOrSteps}\\\\``,\\n      `  - *Expected:* ${t.expectedResult}`,\\n      `  - *Actual:* ${t.actualResult}${t.blockedOrSkippedReason ? ` (Reason: ${t.blockedOrSkippedReason})` : \'\'}`\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  return lines.join(\'\\\\n\');\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/MIHIR/src/lib/workspaceLogic.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding board workflow helpers to workspaceLogic.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add board workflow helpers\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\201\034\n\376\033\001i\024}\023e\240\305\223\372(\n\032O\277\023\324\347LrH\363\025\241\230\373\375[\270\224\fF|m\254\031\232\3049\032V\a\311\262)\031:\257bK#A\320\3733X\241\240\322F\371\252\214Um\206{%\tkX\024\324\fG9\262\325wJ\345\325\303\355h\331k\225\207\250A\243\353b\346\'\210\266\215\t\263L\246z\271\303\255_{5\240I\261(\271\203t\020\263\224d\315\256\\\032\360E\332\231\264\005u\2601\334\316\212\244\257E\n9\251n\330\373\243\\\365&;\232Fmn\332*\230\204c\307\262u\031\374Y\324\v\333\036\251$l\234\226\340\245\321=E\325\'\327\237z6G\225\360;\372\365\223}\216\243\252\274\020\271\350\201(\226\252\367\240O~\264B|Y\3621\1775\334i\225}\371\336V\322o\v\257\222\214\266\372\324&F\"G\a\256\374\211x\255T3\277/){\347\374\237\341\024I\202^oU\212\3009\207r\236\256\333\"E}r\252\343$\310\302\3745\253\340t\325=\230\002\n\235:7;\374T>4oZN\002e\223p+\024\361[4\b\b\025\021\261\020\316\313\277\2243\317\020\205\343\355Qk\002\021\n\317pq\223\345\342y\205\177\361\337%\333\301r\312\203\265\311\261/\204mz51\326\343\375\366J7\320\t\375J\327\242\r\271\252 \000\375\233\346\235X\326\034V.\036\235\201\3254\3709\231 \260\247&\234\273\020\321\227\351\347\005\2508z]\244\316{w\353A\363\264\327\247\3747\037\236L%\0265iX\221\375[\020]\243HT\371u\bOX_b=_\r\322\316\005\265\235L\031\3325\327#\rH\266\004\234Z\355\335\311\311\327\265\240$\306\327\344\203E\021\276\266\2136^\322a\006H\001d\2017\b\301 ^\353\344>c\340+p\f\033\271\377\371v\362{\360\372f\022\220*\016\363Sk\376FOS\242\301d0K\030`\320\307\362c\374\004\364\225\025\222\263+c\261\263\037\255\350\343\231q\f{)p\005\"\237\r\213`4\234\375\242\276\305\230\300E\323\246\300G\247\005^\344 \232\020\213Dg\355\023\275\245Po\313VFD\245\205\347\235\257\330&\226\000m\313\215u\264\017\355.\256~\235\b\350\002\317\212\333\311\217\fA\356\033K\252\257}i\233Y\276\337\272\366/\n\375m\tR\330;\234\177@\330\333\232;,\243\377\374|\210\2640\366\026\212\270i\020*\2548\004\255\273\310\232Z\226:\357\251\250c\034M\244\274\324\a$\212\213\030\345\2352