  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Verification Plan**\n\nI\'m currently focused on outlining the verification plan and architecture. My thoughts revolve around ensuring the seamless functionality of drag-and-drop task reordering, both within and across columns, while meticulously persisting the changes to the backend. This requires a robust plan.\n\n\n**Mapping User Journeys**\n\nI\'ve moved on to mapping out specific user journeys, focusing on drag-and-drop scenarios. Journey 1 details same-column reordering in a 4-column board, including verification of immediate position swaps, confirmation notices, and persistence after reloading. I\'m also planning Journey 2, which covers cross-column drag-and-drop actions, including verifying correct status transitions and index insertions.\n\n\n**Expanding Reordering Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the scope to include reordering in a 7-stage, granular board view. I\'m focusing on ensuring reordering works through accessible move up/down buttons. I\'m also architecting a backend solution, adding `boardOrder` to `TaskRecord` and writing pure functions for sorting tasks and computing reordered lists. I need to ensure the logic handles edge cases and maintains data integrity.\n\n\n**Implementing Reordering Logic**\n\nI\'m now in the thick of implementation! I\'m adding `reorderTasksInColumn` to `/MIHIR/server/db.ts`, which will assign sequential `boardOrder` values to tasks, accommodating status updates and maintaining relative order, as well as updating the `normalizeStoredTask` function. Furthermore, I\'m building the `POST /api/tasks/reorder` endpoint in `/MIHIR/server/apiRouter.ts`, which will handle requests with ordered task IDs, target status, moved task ID, and column labels. It calls `reorderTasksInColumn`, logs an activity item, and returns the updated task and workspace state.\n\n\n**Adding Drag-and-Drop**\n\nI\'m currently integrating drag-and-drop functionality into the application. Specifically, I\'m adding `handleReorderTasks` to `MihirWorkspaceApp.tsx`, which handles the API call to `/api/tasks/reorder` and syncs with Firestore if the user is authenticated. Also, I am modifying `TaskListView.tsx` to support card-level drop targets across both board views and determining \'before\'/\'after\' positions based on cursor placement during drags, ensuring deterministic placement during automated testing.\n\n\n**Visualizing Insertion Points**\n\nI\'m now focused on the visual cues for drag-and-drop. I\'m adding a clear insertion line above or below target cards during drag-over. Furthermore, I\'ll add accessible Move Up/Down buttons with appropriate ARIA labels and test IDs. I\'m also including order badges on cards in columns with multiple tasks. I\'m checking the behavior of Playwright\'s `dragAndDrop` function. It seems that dropping on the center of the target element might lead to unexpected reordering based on the source and target indices. I need to handle this correctly.\n\n\n"
