  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `sortTasksByBoardOrder` and `computeReorderedColumnTaskIds` functions. My immediate task is to introduce a `boardOrder` property to the `TaskRecord` type within `/MIHIR/src/types/workspace.ts`, as a preliminary step in understanding the data structures involved.\n\n\n**Analyzing Sort Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the `sortTasksByBoardOrder` function. My approach involves understanding how tasks with explicit `boardOrder` values should be prioritized during sorting, while also managing tasks without this property. I\'m considering using the `boardOrder` for sorting, if it exists, and maintaining relative positioning for tasks without a specified order. This focuses on sorting tasks by board order.\n\n\n**Refining Drag-and-Drop**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the drag-and-drop implementation. My focus has shifted to cross-column interactions, specifically the logic around appending the `draggedTaskId` to the end of a column when a drop occurs on the column background. I\'m also refining the placement determination logic, particularly addressing scenarios where a card is dropped directly at the center of another card, considering `offsetY` values in `TaskListView.tsx`.\n\n\n**Tracing Algorithm Steps**\n\nI\'m now tracing the `computeReorderedColumnTaskIds` function with concrete examples. Specifically, I\'m analyzing a scenario involving moving `task-1` before `task-3` in the \'Review\' column, focusing on how `sourceIndex` and `targetIndex` influence the insertion point. I\'m carefully evaluating the impact of the `\'before\'` or `\'auto\'` `dropPosition` on the effective insertion index. I am now proceeding with the algorithm steps.\n\n\n**Implementing Reordering Logic**\n\nI\'m now detailing the backend persistence logic to support the drag-and-drop feature. I\'m focusing on the `reorderTasksInColumn` function, specifically, how it should manage task reordering and status updates. I\'ve designed an implementation where `boardOrder` reflects the updated order, and status is updated if different values are provided.\n\n\n"
