  planner_response {
    response: "`TaskListView` and the workspace backend have been enhanced to support drag-and-drop task reordering within the same status column (as well as targeted positional drops across columns), persisting the new order to the backend.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n- **Same-Column & Positional Drag-and-Drop Reordering**:\n  - Added card-level drop target detection (`before` / `after`) with visual insertion indicators (`Drop before ...` / `Drop after ...`) and rank indicators (`#1`, `#2`, etc.) in both the **4-Column Workflow** (`Todo`, `In Progress`, `Review`, `Done`) and **7-Stage Granular** board views.\n  - Added accessible **Move Up / Move Down** controls (`\342\206\221` / `\342\206\223`) on cards in columns with multiple tasks for keyboard and single-click reordering.\n- **Pure Ordering Logic & Unit Tests**:\n  - Added `boardOrder` to `TaskRecord` along with `sortTasksByBoardOrder` and `computeReorderedColumnTaskIds` in `workspaceLogic.ts`, verified by unit tests in `workspaceLogic.test.ts`.\n- **Backend Persistence**:\n  - Added `reorderTasksInColumn` in `server/db.ts` and the `POST /api/tasks/reorder` endpoint in `server/apiRouter.ts` to persist sequential `boardOrder` values in SQLite, log reorder events to the activity log, and sync updated tasks to Cloud Firestore when signed in."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Layout Changes**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the visual layout, specifically focusing on `board-reordered-desktop.png`. I\'m pleased with the placement. `#1 MIHIR-001` anchors the left, with `High [\342\206\221 \342\206\223]` on the right. \"Ready for Testing\" and \"Ray\" fit nicely below the title, improving readability.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "`TaskListView` and the workspace backend have been enhanced to support drag-and-drop task reordering within the same status column (as well as targeted positional drops across columns), persisting the new order to the backend.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n- **Same-Column & Positional Drag-and-Drop Reordering**:\n  - Added card-level drop target detection (`before` / `after`) with visual insertion indicators (`Drop before ...` / `Drop after ...`) and rank indicators (`#1`, `#2`, etc.) in both the **4-Column Workflow** (`Todo`, `In Progress`, `Review`, `Done`) and **7-Stage Granular** board views.\n  - Added accessible **Move Up / Move Down** controls (`\342\206\221` / `\342\206\223`) on cards in columns with multiple tasks for keyboard and single-click reordering.\n- **Pure Ordering Logic & Unit Tests**:\n  - Added `boardOrder` to `TaskRecord` along with `sortTasksByBoardOrder` and `computeReorderedColumnTaskIds` in `workspaceLogic.ts`, verified by unit tests in `workspaceLogic.test.ts`.\n- **Backend Persistence**:\n  - Added `reorderTasksInColumn` in `server/db.ts` and the `POST /api/tasks/reorder` endpoint in `server/apiRouter.ts` to persist sequential `boardOrder` values in SQLite, log reorder events to the activity log, and sync updated tasks to Cloud Firestore when signed in."
