  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 4
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Core Request**: Update the \"Create New Developer Task\" (`NewTaskModal.tsx`) and repository/branch workflow configuration across the application based on the user\'s prompt and two attached screenshots (`/public/assets/aistudio/image_e9d9639d.png` and `/public/assets/aistudio/image_40f88281.png`):\n     1. **Auto-assigned Task ID**: Ensure the Task ID (`MIHIR-005`, etc.) is automatically assigned (auto-generated and synced whenever `NewTaskModal` opens or tasks change, and displayed as an auto-assigned read-only/auto-badged ID so the user doesn\'t have to manually type it, or auto-populated and locked/auto-managed).\n     2. **All 7 Ray Repositories + Inline \"Add Repo / Custom Folder\" Option**:\n        - Screenshot 2 (`/public/assets/aistudio/image_40f88281.png`) shows the user\'s 7 actual Ray repositories/folders:\n          1. `rayapp`\n          2. `raydashboard`\n          3. `raydashboard-power-btn-fix`\n          4. `raygateway`\n          5. `rayhubapp`\n          6. `rayhubdashboard`\n          7. `rayjobapp`\n        - Seed and ensure all 7 of these repositories exist in the workspace (both in `seedAssets.ts` and upgraded/ensured in `server/db.ts` for existing SQLite databases so all 7 appear immediately without needing a DB reset).\n        - In `NewTaskModal.tsx` (and wherever repos are selected), add an inline option to **add a new repository / custom folder** directly inside the modal (`+ Add Repo / Custom Folder`), persisted to the backend (`/api/repositories`) or task configuration.\n     3. **Remove the Showing of Folder Paths (`localFolderPath`)**:\n        - \"also remove the list of the showing folders\" \342\200\224 In `NewTaskModal.tsx` (line 359\342\200\223361: `<span className=\"font-mono text-slate-500 truncate max-w-xs\">{repoObj?.localFolderPath}</span>`) and in repository/branch cards, remove the displayed `/Users/mihir/workspace/ray/...` local folder path list/text that clutters the UI, while allowing the user to add a custom repo/folder name when needed.\n     4. **Remove `Dev Target Branch` \342\200\224 Keep Only Two Branches (`Base Branch` and `Working Branch`)**:\n        - \"in the brach section remove the dev target brach i need only two base branch and the working branch\"\n        - In `NewTaskModal.tsx` (lines 363\342\200\223394) and `TaskDetailView.tsx` / `ProjectsReposView.tsx`, remove the `Dev Target` (`devTargetBranch`) input/display from the branch configuration section so each selected repository shows **only two branch fields**: **Base Branch** and **Working Branch** (in a clean 2-column grid `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2`).\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed Previously**:\n     - Added 4-column workflow drag-and-drop Board View (`Todo`, `In Progress`, `Review`, `Done`) and same-column drag-and-drop reordering with SQLite persistence (`POST /api/tasks/reorder`, `reorderTasksInColumn` in `/MIHIR/server/db.ts`).\n   - **Completed in Current Turn**:\n     - Viewed both user-attached images:\n       - `/public/assets/aistudio/image_e9d9639d.png`: Shows the `Task ID` input field with `MIHIR-005`.\n       - `/public/assets/aistudio/image_40f88281.png`: Shows the 7 folders in the user\'s file manager: `rayapp`, `raydashboard`, `raydashboard-power-btn-fix`, `raygateway`, `rayhubapp`, `rayhubdashboard`, `rayjobapp`.\n     - Inspected `/MIHIR/src/components/NewTaskModal.tsx` (lines 1\342\200\223420) and `/MIHIR/server/seedAssets.ts` (lines 1\342\200\223160).\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - **Bug in `NewTaskModal.tsx` for Auto-Assigned Task ID**:\n     - Currently in `/MIHIR/src/components/NewTaskModal.tsx`, `const [taskCode, setTaskCode] = useState(suggestedTaskCode);` only initializes once when `NewTaskModal` first mounts because `<NewTaskModal>` is rendered unconditionally at the bottom of `MihirWorkspaceApp.tsx` (`isOpen={newTaskOpen}`). When `suggestedTaskCode` updates or when the modal reopens, `taskCode` and `selectedRepos` can hold stale values, and the input is editable instead of clearly auto-assigned!\n     - Adding a `useEffect` in `NewTaskModal.tsx` when `isOpen` or `suggestedTaskCode` changes to automatically set `taskCode = suggestedTaskCode` (and making the Task ID field `readOnly` with an `\"Auto\"` badge, while also updating `workingBranch` defaults) guarantees that Task ID is always auto-assigned (`MIHIR-005`, `MIHIR-006`, etc.).\n   - **Existing SQLite DB Upgrade for the 7 Repositories**:\n     - Because `/MIHIR/data/mihir_workspace.sqlite` is already initialized on disk with only 3 repositories (`raydashboard`, `rayhubapp`, `rayjobapp`), we must both update `DEFAULT_RAY_REPOSITORIES` in `/MIHIR/server/seedAssets.ts` AND run a startup migration helper `ensureDefaultRepositories()` in `/MIHIR/server/db.ts` that inserts the missing 4 repositories (`rayapp`, `raydashboard-power-btn-fix`, `raygateway`, `rayhubdashboard`) into the `repositories` table if they don\'t exist yet.\n   - **Inline Custom Repo / Folder Creation in `NewTaskModal.tsx`**:\n     - `NewTaskModal` should receive `onSaveRepository?: (payload: Partial<RepositoryConfig>) => Promise<void>` (or create & select a custom repo/folder inline) so the user can click `+ Add Repo / Custom Folder` right inside the \"Target Repositories & Branch Configuration\" section, enter a repo/folder name (and optional default base branch), and immediately add it to the workspace and select it for the task.\n\n4. **Active Context**\n   - Dev server is running on `http://localhost:3000`.\n   - Relevant files to inspect/edit next:\n     - `/MIHIR/server/seedAssets.ts` (lines 146\342\200\223220)\n     - `/MIHIR/server/db.ts` (startup `ensureDefaultRepositories` so existing DB gets all 7 repos)\n     - `/MIHIR/src/components/NewTaskModal.tsx` (auto-assigned Task ID, inline `+ Add Repo / Custom Folder`, remove `localFolderPath` display, remove `Dev Target` branch input leaving only `Base Branch` and `Working Branch`)\n     - `/MIHIR/src/MihirWorkspaceApp.tsx` (pass `onSaveRepository={handleSaveRepository}` and `suggestedTaskCode` to `NewTaskModal`, and reset form state on task creation)\n     - `/MIHIR/src/components/TaskDetailView.tsx` and `/MIHIR/src/components/ProjectsReposView.tsx` (check where `devTargetBranch` and `localFolderPath` are shown and clean them up to match the user\'s preference).\n\n5. **Next Steps**\n   1. View the rest of `/MIHIR/server/seedAssets.ts` (lines 160\342\200\223230), `/MIHIR/src/components/NewTaskModal.tsx` (lines 420\342\200\223506), `/MIHIR/src/MihirWorkspaceApp.tsx` (lines 1115\342\200\2231169), `/MIHIR/src/components/TaskDetailView.tsx`, and `/MIHIR/src/components/ProjectsReposView.tsx`.\n   2. Update `/MIHIR/server/seedAssets.ts` and `/MIHIR/server/db.ts` so all 7 repositories (`rayapp`, `raydashboard`, `raydashboard-power-btn-fix`, `raygateway`, `rayhubapp`, `rayhubdashboard`, `rayjobapp`) are seeded and automatically ensured in the SQLite `repositories` table.\n   3. Update `/MIHIR/src/components/NewTaskModal.tsx`:\n      - Make `Task ID` auto-assigned (`readOnly`, synced via `useEffect` with `suggestedTaskCode` when modal opens, styled with an `Auto` indicator).\n      - Show all 7 repositories as selectable pills plus an inline `+ Add Repo / Custom Folder` form so users can add any custom repo/folder right from the modal.\n      - Remove the `localFolderPath` display list from selected repositories.\n      - Remove the `Dev Target` branch field so only **Base Branch** and **Working Branch** are shown (in a 2-column layout).\n   4. Also check `TaskDetailView.tsx` and `ProjectsReposView.tsx` to remove `Dev Target` branch and folder path clutter where appropriate.\n   5. Run unit tests (`npx tsx --test ...`), `compile_applet`, `lint_applet`, `restart_dev_server`, and verify in a real headless browser via `playwright-cli` (including screenshots inspected with `view_file`).\n\n6. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Follow `ultra-mode` verification loop: unit test pure logic, compile/lint, restart dev server, and visually inspect the rendered UI in `playwright-cli` using `view_file` on screenshots.\n   - Maintain compatibility with `firebase-integration-rpc` security rules.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 278
    included_step_index_end: 370
