  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Intent**\n\nI\'m currently meticulously examining the user\'s request and our verification plan. I\'m focusing specifically on the auto-assignment of task IDs, diving into the `NewTaskModal.tsx` file to pinpoint the relevant code for verification. The aim is to ensure the implementation precisely aligns with the user\'s intent.\n\n\n**Implementing Task ID Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the automated Task ID assignment. My focus has shifted to the backend logic, specifically the `/api/tasks` endpoint. The goal is to ensure that `taskCode` is automatically assigned if missing, or handle duplicates. I\'m also planning a helper function in `src/lib/workspaceLogic.ts` and will write comprehensive unit tests.\n\n\n**Defining Default Repositories**\n\nI\'ve decided on defining `DEFAULT_RAY_REPOSITORIES` within `/MIHIR/server/seedAssets.ts`. It will include configurations for all seven repositories. I plan to call `ensureDefaultRepositories()` during startup in `/MIHIR/server/db.ts` to ensure existing SQLite databases populate with all repos without data loss. I\'m also adding a new button in `NewTaskModal.tsx` and `TaskDetailView.tsx` to handle adding custom repositories via `POST /api/repositories`. Finally, I\'m removing the display of folder paths.\n\n\n**Refining UI Display**\n\nI\'m removing the folder path display from several components: `NewTaskModal.tsx`, `TaskDetailView.tsx` (Section B), and `ProjectsReposView.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m removing the `<span className=\"font-mono text-slate-500 truncate max-w-xs\">{repoObj?.localFolderPath}</span>` element in `NewTaskModal.tsx` and the other mentioned components. Additionally, I\'m removing the \"Dev Target\" branch field from the branch section in `NewTaskModal.tsx`, leaving only \"Base Branch\" and \"Working Branch\" inputs.\n\n\n"
