    thinking: "**Analyzing Modal Behavior**\n\nI\'ve been examining `NewTaskModal.tsx`. The key is understanding how the modal responds to the `isOpen` prop. Initially, the `taskCode` state was only set once.\n\n\n**Addressing User Requests**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating the user\'s feature requests. I need to ensure automatic task ID assignment, the option to add a repository and a custom folder, and remove the folder list. I\'m also removing the \"dev\" target branch, leaving only base and working branches. I\'m looking at `TaskGitWorkflowSection.tsx` for relevant code.\n\n\n**Refining UI Display**\n\nI\'m now honing the display of repository and branch information within `TaskGitWorkflowSection.tsx`. I\'ll remove hardcoded folder paths and the \"dev\" branch display, showing just \"Repository: <repositoryName>\" and \"Base: <baseBranch> \342\206\222 Working: <workingBranch>\". This should provide a cleaner presentation. I also am looking at `seedAssets.ts` to export `DEFAULT_RAY_REPOSITORIES: RepositoryConfig[]` which should contain all 7 repositories.\n\n\n**Defining Repository Defaults**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the default Ray repositories from the provided screenshot. I need to define the repository configurations, ensuring the base branches are set correctly. I\'ll include the repository name as the `localFolderPath`. I\'m going to add a new function, `ensureDefaultRepositories()`, to `/MIHIR/server/db.ts` to manage this process. It will check existing repositories and add missing defaults after seeding.\n\n\n"
